From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:42:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [boringssl] target.h: recognise ppc64le (portable C, no
 assembly)

include/openssl/target.h ends in #error "Unknown target CPU" for any
CPU it does not list, and BoringSSL at 9f138d05 lists no PowerPC: its
ppc64le assembly was removed upstream. Every BoringSSL translation
unit (and, through it, dart:io's TLS in the engine) fails on ppc64le.

Add a little-endian ppc64 arm that defines OPENSSL_64_BIT and the
OPENSSL_PPC64LE label. No source tests OPENSSL_PPC64LE any more, and
the GAS assembly files are wrapped in per-CPU checks, so this builds
the portable C implementations (all 438 objects of
//flutter/third_party/boringssl build with system clang 22).

Minimal alternative to Debian chromium's
0001-Add-PPC64-support-for-boringssl.patch, which restores the PPC64
assembly. The standalone Dart SDK carries its own BoringSSL checkout and
needs the same one-hunk change (an M1 item for the Dart track).

Class: upstreamable fix in spirit (BoringSSL's comment invites local
patches for unlisted CPUs); carried locally.

Byte-identical to the Dart ppc64 series' BoringSSL patch (0032 in
work/dart-sdk-patches-next), so the engine's BoringSSL tree equals the
Dart tree's (a67ee71b) and one patch serves both.
---
 include/openssl/target.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/third_party/boringssl/src/include/openssl/target.h b/engine/src/flutter/third_party/boringssl/src/include/openssl/target.h
index 8d4763d..3eccaf0 100644
--- a/engine/src/flutter/third_party/boringssl/src/include/openssl/target.h
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/third_party/boringssl/src/include/openssl/target.h
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@
 #define OPENSSL_RISCV64
 #elif defined(__riscv) && __SIZEOF_POINTER__ == 4
 #define OPENSSL_32_BIT
+#elif defined(__powerpc64__) && defined(__LITTLE_ENDIAN__)
+// ppc64le (ELFv2). No assembly: the generic C implementations are used.
+#define OPENSSL_64_BIT
+#define OPENSSL_PPC64LE
 #elif defined(__pnacl__)
 #define OPENSSL_32_BIT
 #define OPENSSL_PNACL
